<%# The recirculation of an article. It has two sections, and each one renders only when it has
    entries: the reports of the same race, and then the related entries, which the api calculates
    from the article text and the concepts (data/related.json, through `rake import:related`).

    ⚠️ The two sections excluded each other before, thus a race with one or two other reports showed
    one or two cards. recirculation_sections removes from the second list each entry that the first
    one holds, thus they can render together and never show the same entry two times.

    ⚠️ scope_entry_ids is necessary: these two sections and read_next render summary cards on this
    same page, and one entry is often in more than one of them. Without the section in the id, two
    cards would have the same DOM id and both aria-labelledby values would point at the first card.
    `article` is a necessary local. %>
<% sections = recirculation_sections(article) %>
<% if sections[:reports].present? %>
  <%= partial 'partials/collection', locals: { title: "More Reports From This Race", items: sections[:reports], variant: "halves", scope_entry_ids: true } %>
<% end %>
<% if sections[:related].present? %>
  <%= partial 'partials/collection', locals: { title: "You May Also Like", items: sections[:related], variant: "halves", scope_entry_ids: true } %>
<% end %>
